risk=critical
This is a binary repackaging of Zoom from an official upstream source, but presents critical supply-chain risks: the PKGBUILD downloads a pre-compiled binary package directly from zoom.us without verification of authenticity (no GPG signature, only SHA512), extracts and repackages it as-is with strip disabled. This pattern is inherently risky because: (1) the upstream binary is opaque and cannot be audited; (2) Zoom is a proprietary application with known security concerns; (3) there is no signature verification to ensure the downloaded binary has not been tampered with in transit; (4) the AUR maintainer is acting as an unverified intermediary for a closed-source application. Even if the current upstream binary is legitimate, this approach offers no protection against man-in-the-middle attacks or upstream compromise.
